# The Open/Save panel inherits the authenticated session namespace.
#
# DELIBERATE, and the most important line of authority in the system to get
# right: the panel browses ON BEHALF of whoever is asking, so it must see
# exactly what the SESSION can see -- the user's writable home plus the
# read-only system and application trees -- and not one directory more.
#
# It must not be narrower than the session, either. A panel that cannot show a
# place the user can reach is a panel that quietly hides their own files, and
# they would have no way to tell that from the file not existing.
#
# What this becomes: once the kernel can pass an open file as a handle
# (kernel/ipc/handle.h knows surfaces, channels, endpoints and pipes today),
# this manifest is what makes the panel a POWERBOX -- a confined application
# with no filesystem namespace of its own could still open exactly the file the
# user pointed at here, because the authority would travel with the handle
# rather than with the path. Recorded in docs/TODO.md.
